-
-## Background (1 paragraph)
-
-The campaign has formalised, on `geometric-ralph`, the local core of the differential-geometric
-Frobenius theorem: rectification (flow-box), the "algebraic miracle" (involutive ⇒ commuting
-basis), the infinitesimal commutator, the **variational equation** (`flow_deriv_firstOrder`), and —
-just now — the **flows-commute bridge**:
-
-    flowsCommute_unconditional_onBox : CommonFlowDomain f g x₀ →
-      (∀ y ∈ box, lieBracket f g y = 0) →
-      ∃ δ, ∀ t s, |t| < δ → |s| < δ → Φₜ (Ψₛ y) = Ψₛ (Φₜ y)   (* bracket=0 ⇒ flows commute *)
-
-This is in `DynamicalSystems/Control/Geometric/FlowTransport.lean` (see also
-`FlowCommutator.lean` for `CommonFlowDomain`, `uniformFlowInvariance`).
-
-## What remains: the Krener lemma (simultaneous rectification)
-
-Prove that `k` pointwise-linearly-independent, pairwise bracket-vanishing vector fields
-`f : Fin k → X → X` are **simultaneously rectifiable**: there is a local diffeomorphism
-`Ψ : (Fin k → ℝ) × Y → X` (`Y` = a complement of `span {f i x₀}`) with `Ψ 0 = x₀` such that each
-coordinate line `t ↦ Ψ (Function.update tᵢ t)` is an integral curve of `f i` — all `k` fields
-straightened at once. (G2 currently has only `krenerLemma_base`, the k=1 case; this is the general
-`krenerLemma`.)
-
-## The classical route (everything it needs is already in the library)
-
-1. Define `F (t : Fin k → ℝ) (z : Y) = Φ₀^{t₀} ∘ … ∘ Φ_{k-1}^{t_{k-1}} (x₀ + ι z)`, where `Φᵢ` is
-   `localFlow (hfᵢ)` and `ι : Y →L[ℝ] X` embeds the complement. Order is immaterial because the
-   flows commute (G12).
-2. `DF 0` is invertible: `∂F/∂tᵢ|₀ = f i x₀` (each flow has time derivative `f i` at 0 —
-   `flowStrictFDerivAt`/`flow_deriv_at_zero`), `∂F/∂z|₀ = ι`, and together they span `X`. Apply
-   `HasStrictFDerivAt.toOpenPartialHomeomorph` to get the local diffeo `Ψ`.
-3. Trajectory rectification: each `t ↦ F (update tᵢ (tᵢ+t)) z` is an integral curve of `f i`
-   (flow property + commutation). This is `krenerLemma`.
-
