+## Chart and regularity results to preserve
+
+`simultaneousRectifyingChart hf hind hcomm` is an `OpenPartialHomeomorph` from
+`(Fin k → ℝ) × frameComplement (fun i => f i x₀)` into `X`.
+
+- `simultaneousRectifyingChart_zero`: the chart sends zero to `x₀`.
+- `zero_mem_simultaneousRectifyingChart_source`: zero belongs to its source.
+- `simultaneousRectifyingChart_contDiffOn`: the chart is `C¹` on its source.
+- `simultaneousRectifyingChart_symm_contDiffOn`: its inverse is `C¹` on its target.
+- `simultaneousRectifyingChart_fderiv`: each time coordinate vector maps to its
+  corresponding vector field throughout the source.
+- `simultaneousRectifyingChart_rectifies`: for `p` in the chart source,
+  `t ↦ Ψ (Function.update p.1 i t, p.2)` has derivative `f i (Ψ p)` at `p.1 i`.
+  Source membership is the only extra domain premise; the chart restriction
+  already supplies the required local-flow conditions.
+
+These regularity theorems justify calling this a `C¹` local diffeomorphism.
+The canonical finite-coordinate conclusion remains `SimultaneouslyRectifiable`.
